# Byte fidelity is the whole point of this repository.
#
# It holds the raw evidence a published paper cites: 24 run folders of
# transcripts and CLI self-reports, sealed acceptance fixtures, oracle outputs,
# and calibration JSON. Several of those are parsed, hashed, or compared
# byte-for-byte (prompt SHA-256 per run; the differential-fuzz and mutation
# result files; `tools/paper_data.py` reads values out of them). A line-ending
# rewrite on checkout or commit would silently alter evidence that a conclusion
# rests on, and it would do it without failing.
#
# So: no end-of-line conversion, in either direction, for anything.
# This is deliberate and is NOT the usual `* text=auto` default.
* -text

# Git's own binary detection still applies to these; marking them keeps a
# diff of a 2 MB transcript from being attempted by accident.
*.jsonl -diff
